      "id": 1,
      "text": "Grampian Pennsylvania takes its name from the Grampian Mountains in Scotland, the ancestral home of an early settler.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grampian%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits amid the Grampian Hills, five miles from Curwensville, and marks the end of the historic Tyrone & Clearfield Branch of the Pennsylvania Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pagenweb.org/~clearfield/individual%20boroughs/grampian.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Grampian reflects its past today, with historic landmarks and traditions still visible in the community’s character and culture.",
